# Third-party material in this repository

## What is retained, and why

`data/raw/` holds items captured from the public feeds registered in
`policy/sources.yaml`. Each item is stored as JSON with the fields the feed
supplied: `title`, `url`, `published`, `source`, and `summary`.

It is committed rather than discarded because the whole claim of this project is
that a reader can check why an article says what it says. Verdicts in
`data/verified/` cite evidence; the raw capture is what the pipeline actually saw
at the time, timestamped, before anything was written about it. Deleting it would
make the audit trail unverifiable a week later.

Copyright in that material belongs to the publishers who produced it. It is not
relicensed by this repository (see LICENSE §3).

## Known limitation

Some publishers put a full article body in the feed's `summary` field rather than
a lede. Where that happens, the retained item is longer than a citation needs to
be. Truncation at ingest is planned; it does not change the position below.

## Removal requests

If you publish a feed represented here and want items removed or truncated, open
an issue at https://github.com/y-nihat/noiseless-news/issues naming the source,
and it will be removed from the working tree and the source retired or capped in
`policy/sources.yaml`.

Note that this repository's history is public and append-only, so removal from
the current tree does not by itself erase earlier commits. If a request requires
history rewriting, say so in the issue and it will be handled.

## Robots and crawling

Ingest fetches only registered feed URLs, at most once per scheduled run, rate
limited per source (3s for arXiv per its API terms; 60s for the Reddit feeds;
1s otherwise), and identifies itself as `noiseless-news/0.1` with a link to this
repository. It does not crawl beyond the registered URLs.
